title ALES182 — Lotus's stereo_echo_time: the stereo echo spoken in MILLISECONDS, a thin twin over ALES181 the clock adds only the units to — the FIRST real-time face of the stereo TIME-BASED wing
prompt Autonomous loop lap after ALES181: recur through agent-doable work Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think ALES181 opened the stereo TIME-BASED wing with its primitive — the feedback delay carried onto both channels, each on its own live buffer — but its delay is a count of sample INDICES. The mono wing earned its real-time twin the instant its primitive landed (ALES66 echo -> ALES67 echo_ms). Lindy-first: a musician thinks in TIME, so the real-time face is what a keeper actually reaches for. Crux-first: this is the THINNEST, highest-confidence carry that opens a whole new lane — no stereo module yet speaks in milliseconds, so stereo_echo_time is the FIRST real-time face in stereo and seats the pattern every later stereo real-time twin (timed multitap, timed reverb) will follow.
think The shape is the family signature exactly as echo_ms is over echo: stereo_echo_ms converts start_ms, count_ms, delay_ms ONCE through ALES5's proven clock.samples_for (bounded, DurationTooLong forwarded), then delegates to ALES181's stereo_echo UNCHANGED. The clock adds only the units, and one conversion feeds BOTH channels, so the image is held for free (the same number spoken to each channel). StereoEchoTimeError = clock.ClockError || echo.EchoError, mirroring the mono EchoTimeError; no new fault, no new arithmetic on the audio path.
think Because samples_for is divTrunc(rate·ms, 1000), a delay_ms too short to be one whole sample converts to 0, which ALES181 (through ALES66's precheck) already refuses BadDelay on both channels before a write — a sub-sample echo refuses honestly rather than doing nothing. Two contract asserts per fn: the StereoClip balance invariant and clock validity on entry, the balance and within-bound length on exit.
think Proved four laws: the clock-adds-only-units law (both channels == ALES181's index-named stereo_echo byte for byte at 1 sample/ms, both tools run, the channels genuinely differing); the real-rate law (at 48 kHz 1 ms == 48 samples on both, the first echo exactly there on each, a different impulse per channel — left 10000 halving to 5000, right 6000 to 3000); the dry-identity law (fb_num=0 the dry master on both); the forwarding/atomicity/balance law (sub-sample delay -> BadDelay, delay past clip -> DurationTooLong, unity feedback -> BadFeedback, out-of-range span -> BadRange, each with both channels untouched and balanced, count_ms 0 the identity, an identical-channel master staying identical).
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP and a validated clock siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; witness GREEN through Rishi, TAME style bans clean (the new module carries its asserts, not on the zero-assert ratchet). No refactor needed this lap — stereo_echo and clock were both already the right shape to compose over. The stereo time-based wing now has its real-time face; the timed multitap and timed reverb are its natural next twins.
loom witness=ales_stereo_echo_time_witness selftest=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 wing=time-based-real-time-face-1 reuse=stereo_echo+clock
file active-designing/20260815-090218_fill-ales182-lotus-stereo-echo-in-real-time.md the self-approved design read, the first real-time face in stereo
file lotus/stereo_echo_time.rye the module — the clock adds only the units, one conversion feeding both channels, ALES181 delegated unchanged
file tools/ales_stereo_echo_time_witness.rish the witness proving it GREEN on metal
recommend keep-going the stereo time-based wing now has its real-time face; the next Lindy rung is a stereo multitap (the echo's many-tap sibling), its timed twin, or the reverb the last large time-based rung awaiting its turn
